1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,481
The Big Bad Wolf: red glowing eyes, terrible noises, and very bad breath.

2
00:00:04,701 --> 00:00:05,981
Here's how it plays.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,896
There's no special setup for the Wolf. It starts with nine health, in Track mode.

4
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,775
The Wolf is always in one of two modes, Track or Slay, each with its own icon.

5
00:00:15,995 --> 00:00:19,058
Most of its Terror cards have different effects for each mode.

6
00:00:19,058 --> 00:00:22,961
At the start of the Killer phase, check which mode it's in, and apply only that

7
00:00:22,961 --> 00:00:24,592
mode's lines, ignoring the other.

8
00:00:24,812 --> 00:00:28,225
Effects without a mode icon always apply, whichever mode it's in.

9
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:33,279
The Wolf starts in Track mode. When its Dark Power is revealed, it switches to Slay

10
00:00:33,279 --> 00:00:33,535
mode.

11
00:00:33,755 --> 00:00:37,908
If that happens during a Killer phase that started in Track mode, keep using Track

12
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:41,605
effects for the rest of that phase. Slay effects start next Killer phase.

13
00:00:41,825 --> 00:00:46,067
The only exception is the Epic Dark Power, A Killing Machine, which makes it resolve

14
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:48,844
both the Track and Slay lines for the rest of the game.

15
00:00:49,667 --> 00:00:53,927
Take The Claws That Scratch. In Track mode, the Wolf targets the closest Victim, or

16
00:00:53,927 --> 00:00:56,237
you if you're closer, and moves towards them.

17
00:00:56,237 --> 00:01:00,138
Then Bloodlust rises once for you and each Victim in its space, up to three.

18
00:01:00,138 --> 00:01:01,421
The Slay line is ignored.

19
00:01:01,641 --> 00:01:06,160
In Slay mode, it still goes after the closest target, but then attacks, dealing its

20
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:09,210
damage one point at a time to as many Victims as it can.

21
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:12,585
If you're in the space, you take whatever damage is left over.

22
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:17,805
Its Dark Powers: Destructive Roar removes the top card of the Item deck closest to

23
00:01:17,805 --> 00:01:20,760
the Wolf from the game, when revealed and every Upkeep.

24
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:25,125
Ravenous Hunger places it in the space with the most Victims and kills them all.

25
00:01:25,125 --> 00:01:28,959
And Sixth Sense makes it ignore damage from Reaction cards like Retaliate.

26
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:32,208
Its Minor Dark Powers are the fairytale lines.

27
00:01:32,208 --> 00:01:36,295
What big ears you have: entering or starting in its space costs you a health.

28
00:01:36,515 --> 00:01:39,627
What big eyes: the same, but you discard a random Action card.

29
00:01:39,627 --> 00:01:43,694
What big teeth: if it attacks you and you block all the damage, you lose a health

30
00:01:43,694 --> 00:01:44,045
anyway.

31
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:48,102
Its Finales: Tasty Treats heals it one for every dead Victim.

32
00:01:48,102 --> 00:01:50,755
Thrill of the Hunt heals it one whenever it moves.

33
00:01:50,975 --> 00:01:54,781
Rampant Growth attacks twice and raises your Horror each time it hits you.

34
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:58,228
And the Epic Finale, One More Bite, always finds someone to attack.

35
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:03,101
A few tips. Track mode is your window: it hurts with Bloodlust, not damage, so

36
00:02:03,101 --> 00:02:03,727
attack then.

37
00:02:03,947 --> 00:02:06,605
Once it's in Slay mode, keep Victims out of its reach:

38
00:02:06,605 --> 00:02:07,787
it tears through groups.

39
00:02:08,007 --> 00:02:11,510
And Sixth Sense can make Retaliate useless, so don't build around it.

40
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:12,017
Good luck.

